1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:03,563
[Man On TV]
Collins working on King here,
top of the key-

2
00:00:03,643 --> 00:00:06,548
dribbling around him,
coming around the corner there, he's up.!

3
00:00:06,618 --> 00:00:09,056
[Crowd Cheering On TV]
Two points.! Beautiful play.

4
00:00:09,124 --> 00:00:11,095
Now, that's a great play.

5
00:00:11,163 --> 00:00:13,635
If you testify, no one can protect you,

6
00:00:13,704 --> 00:00:15,641
especially the feds.

7
00:00:15,709 --> 00:00:18,113
- We'll keep you safe, Joey.
- Right. In Witness Protection.

8
00:00:18,182 --> 00:00:19,948
This great new life he's giving you?

9
00:00:20,020 --> 00:00:22,891
You're sackin' groceries
at some goat-town Stop and Shop,

10
00:00:22,961 --> 00:00:26,197
when one of Vitale's guys comes
and puts two in the back of your skull.

11
00:00:26,271 --> 00:00:30,008
Counselor, are you advising a witness
to withhold evidence
from a federal grand jury?

12
00:00:30,081 --> 00:00:32,018
He came forward.
He volunteered.

13
00:00:32,086 --> 00:00:35,858
I'm advising him not to testify
until I'm satisfied you can protect him.

14
00:00:35,929 --> 00:00:38,595
Hey, you guys mind?
I got money on this.

15
00:00:38,671 --> 00:00:41,075
What do you want?
We gave you everything you asked for.

16
00:00:41,144 --> 00:00:44,482
- I asked for pasta.
- You got steak. Enjoy it.

17
00:00:47,060 --> 00:00:48,997
- What are you doin'?
- What?

18
00:00:50,937 --> 00:00:53,877
Where's your quit candy?
I just gave you a pack.
Yeah, sorry.

19
00:00:53,945 --> 00:00:56,782
I forgot.

20
00:00:56,853 --> 00:00:58,790
Joey, whatever they give us,

21
00:00:58,858 --> 00:01:01,798
what they tell you,
you get popped,
what am I gonna do, sue them?

22
00:01:02,936 --> 00:01:04,873
That's not what this is about.

23
00:01:05,978 --> 00:01:08,074
You're gonna miss me.

24
00:01:08,150 --> 00:01:10,485
- I'm your lawyer, Joey.
- You're my brother.

25
00:01:11,726 --> 00:01:15,132
And I do this-you know,
I go into Witness Protection-

26
00:01:15,202 --> 00:01:17,332
we're never gonna
see each other again.

27
00:01:18,880 --> 00:01:21,250
- That doesn't bother you?
- It kills me.

28
00:01:24,729 --> 00:01:27,600
[Man On TV]
There he goes. Nice pick.

29
00:01:27,670 --> 00:01:30,974
[Continues, Indistinct]

30
00:01:31,045 --> 00:01:33,643
I gotta take a leak.

31
00:01:35,458 --> 00:01:38,398
- [Groans]
- You all right?

32
00:01:41,039 --> 00:01:45,814
Yeah, yeah.
Just, uh, a little dizzy.

33
00:01:45,886 --> 00:01:48,552
Get some air.
Hot.

34
00:01:50,932 --> 00:01:53,632
- Joey.
- What'd you say to him?

35
00:01:53,707 --> 00:01:56,544
Yeah, nice try.
Come on!
Let go of me!

36
00:01:56,615 --> 00:01:58,985
- Let go of me!
Can't you see he's sick?
- Joey!

37
00:01:59,054 --> 00:02:01,618
Let me go.!
Something's wrong with him.!

38
00:02:01,694 --> 00:02:03,562
You're not getting out
of this that easy.
Joey.

39
00:02:03,634 --> 00:02:06,072
Either you're dead or you're testifying.

40
00:02:40,199 --> 00:02:42,136
[Cuddy]
Don't have it.

41
00:02:42,204 --> 00:02:44,802
[Vogler] Budget?
Nope.

42
00:02:44,878 --> 00:02:47,316
Revenue statement. List of expenses.

43
00:02:47,385 --> 00:02:49,322
House has been very busy.

44
00:02:49,391 --> 00:02:51,920
Saving New Jersey from leprosy.
Yes, I know.

45
00:02:51,997 --> 00:02:55,062
Getting me his numbers,
that's your job.

46
00:02:55,139 --> 00:02:58,307
- We're in a meeting.
- I need the lawyer.

47
00:02:58,381 --> 00:03:01,651
Who'd you kill?
Nobody. But it's not even lunch.

48
00:03:01,724 --> 00:03:04,698
I got served with a federal court order.
Some witness went into a coma.

49
00:03:04,765 --> 00:03:06,702
They want me to take a look at him.

50
00:03:06,770 --> 00:03:08,536
What?

51
00:03:08,608 --> 00:03:12,345
They want you
to examine a sick person?

52
00:03:12,419 --> 00:03:14,549
This is a public relations nightmare.

53
00:03:14,625 --> 00:03:16,823
Folk think our staff do
that kind of thing around here,

54
00:03:16,897 --> 00:03:19,369
this place will be crawling
with sick people.

55
00:03:19,438 --> 00:03:22,742
I'm a doctor. I'm not a lapdog
for the feds. I don't play fetch.

56
00:03:22,813 --> 00:03:26,984
Nobody tells you what to do.
Am I right, Dr. Cuddy?

57
00:03:27,059 --> 00:03:31,332
You have three choices.
Hire a lawyer to fight the order,
treat the guy or go to jail for contempt.

58
00:03:31,403 --> 00:03:33,738
Up to you.

59
00:03:33,810 --> 00:03:38,220
Jail. You'd like that.
No more naughty schoolgirl.

60
00:03:38,289 --> 00:03:40,784
Conjugal visit- that's her new fantasy.

61
00:03:46,277 --> 00:03:49,878
[Sighs]
We're not leaving until he's gone,
or you show me...

62
00:03:49,954 --> 00:03:53,224
one good reason for keeping him.

63
00:04:10,543 --> 00:04:13,175
[Beeping, Whirring]

64
00:04:17,361 --> 00:04:19,298
He's really out of it, huh?

65
00:04:21,238 --> 00:04:24,576
Causes of coma-
metabolic, structural-
He had his stomach pumped.

66
00:04:24,648 --> 00:04:27,143
Why would they do that?
Rule out poisoning.

67
00:04:27,221 --> 00:04:29,158
Huh.
Not the typical first guess.

68
00:04:29,226 --> 00:04:33,967
Nope, first guess was faking it.
The patient's a federal witness-
reluctant, I'm assuming.

69
00:04:34,040 --> 00:04:36,102
He's also an eight on
the Glasgow Coma Scale.

70
00:04:36,178 --> 00:04:38,548
[Whistles]
He's barely alive.
Pretty tough to fake.

71
00:04:38,618 --> 00:04:41,523
Any recent history of head trauma?
Bad car accident? Fall?

72
00:04:41,593 --> 00:04:43,928
They tell me no,
but do an M.R.I. To be sure.

73
00:04:44,000 --> 00:04:45,971
[Chase]
Metabolic causes-
liver, kidney, diabetes-

74
00:04:46,038 --> 00:04:48,134
Check for everything.
Feds are paying.

75
00:04:48,211 --> 00:04:50,375
We're gonna turn a profit
on this one, boys.

76
00:04:50,451 --> 00:04:53,550
Dr. House, Bill Arnello.
I'm a lawyer.

77
00:04:53,625 --> 00:04:57,066
I represent Mr. Smith.
What's wrong with him?

78
00:04:57,135 --> 00:04:59,333
Do I come to you
with my problems?

79
00:04:59,408 --> 00:05:01,972
He's also my brother.

80
00:05:02,048 --> 00:05:04,246
What? You changed your name?

81
00:05:04,321 --> 00:05:06,759
Smith wasn't good enough for you?

82
00:05:06,827 --> 00:05:09,629
His name's Joey.
He's my only brother.
He's important to you.

83
00:05:09,702 --> 00:05:14,203
Got it. So, no placebos for him.
We'll use the real medicine.
[Elevator Dings]

84
00:05:14,281 --> 00:05:16,309
This was fun.
Let's do it again soon.

85
00:05:21,367 --> 00:05:24,238
Brother in the Mafia?

86
00:05:26,113 --> 00:05:28,984
So, justJoey?

87
00:05:29,054 --> 00:05:31,082
I was hoping for a nickname.

88
00:05:31,160 --> 00:05:34,498
Joey Mango.
Joey the Wrench.

89
00:05:36,508 --> 00:05:39,914
[Bangs]
[Alarm Rings, Stops]

90
00:05:39,984 --> 00:05:43,220
People know where I am.
I want you to do your job.

91
00:05:43,292 --> 00:05:45,958
Diagnose him,
fix him and keep him here.

92
00:05:47,538 --> 00:05:52,279
We're a bit of a specialized hospital.
We generally only deal with patients
while they're actually sick.

93
00:05:52,351 --> 00:05:54,618
If you release my brother
to the government,

94
00:05:54,690 --> 00:05:58,153
and he does what they want,
even if you fix him, he's dead.

95
00:05:58,233 --> 00:06:00,170
I need time to convince him of that.

96
00:06:04,049 --> 00:06:05,986
[Alarm Rings, Stops]

97
00:06:09,330 --> 00:06:11,859
Good news is,
if you screw up,

98
00:06:11,937 --> 00:06:14,272
you don't have to worry
about a malpractice suit.

99
00:06:15,513 --> 00:06:18,954
Instead, one by one,

100
00:06:19,022 --> 00:06:21,859
I'll take away the things you love
till there's nothing left.

101
00:06:22,866 --> 00:06:24,803
[Dings]

102
00:06:27,913 --> 00:06:30,317
So, on the Mafia thing,

103
00:06:30,387 --> 00:06:32,381
that's a yes.

104
00:06:36,270 --> 00:06:38,503
[Whirring]

105
00:06:41,416 --> 00:06:43,888
[Cameron]
Did House seem weird to you?

106
00:06:43,957 --> 00:06:45,894
Were you expecting him
to be weird?

107
00:06:46,898 --> 00:06:49,370
We spoke...

108
00:06:49,438 --> 00:06:51,876
about how we felt.

109
00:06:51,944 --> 00:06:54,644
You told him you liked him?
No, of course not.

110
00:06:54,719 --> 00:06:58,286
Wh-What are you talking about then?
I asked him if he liked me.

111
00:06:58,362 --> 00:07:01,427
Why would you do that?
Because-

112
00:07:02,908 --> 00:07:06,007
[Sighs]
I like him.

113
00:07:06,083 --> 00:07:08,316
You like him like him?

114
00:07:08,389 --> 00:07:10,587
Doesn't matter.
He doesn't like me.

115
00:07:10,662 --> 00:07:14,103
Hey, he doesn't like anybody.

116
00:07:15,743 --> 00:07:17,680
And nobody likes him.

117
00:07:19,185 --> 00:07:21,987
M.R.I. Showed a subdural hematoma.

118
00:07:22,060 --> 00:07:26,162
Bleeding around his brain
caused pressure inside his head,
which caused the coma.

119
00:07:26,238 --> 00:07:28,334
These look like pseudo-membranes.

120
00:07:28,410 --> 00:07:30,347
Those take time to form.

121
00:07:30,416 --> 00:07:32,649
If it's an old injury,
it wouldn't cause the coma.

122
00:07:32,722 --> 00:07:36,824
Patient history indicates he was hit
with a tire iron in 1996.

123
00:07:36,900 --> 00:07:39,270
Brother says he was
changing a tire and it slipped.

124
00:07:39,339 --> 00:07:42,677
An old hematoma
placed where this one is
could have caused his coma.

125
00:07:42,749 --> 00:07:45,551
- What about his liver?
- L.F.T.'s are slightly elevated.

126
00:07:45,623 --> 00:07:48,528
Key word is "slightly,"
as in not high enough
to cause the coma.

127
00:07:48,598 --> 00:07:51,766
It's the subdural.
I say we evacuate the cavity,
see if he wakes up.

128
00:07:51,840 --> 00:07:56,284
The neurologist thinks it's his brain
and wants to open up his head?
Frankly, I'm shocked.

129
00:07:56,352 --> 00:08:00,260
And you get to use the "big boy"drill
in Daddy's big red toolbox.

130
00:08:00,330 --> 00:08:03,064
[Joey]
No drilling.

131
00:08:05,544 --> 00:08:09,111
- Hi.
- Mr. Smith.

132
00:08:09,187 --> 00:08:11,955
Call meJoe.
Can you not do that?

133
00:08:15,504 --> 00:08:19,207
So, we're clear about the no drilling?

134
00:08:21,420 --> 00:08:23,357
[Chase]
He's okay now. He can leave.

135
00:08:23,425 --> 00:08:26,399
I'm not releasing him.
'Cause the brother
doesn't want you to?

136
00:08:26,466 --> 00:08:29,929
Or because he had
an unexplained coma.
Which sounds better?

137
00:08:30,009 --> 00:08:33,542
The hematoma caused the coma.
That's a catchy diagnosis.
You could dance to that.

138
00:08:33,619 --> 00:08:35,886
[Foreman]
I think Chase is right.

139
00:08:39,268 --> 00:08:43,975
It still should be evacuated,
but it's not an immediate threat.

140
00:08:47,825 --> 00:08:49,762
Cameron's my girl.

141
00:08:49,830 --> 00:08:51,926
I'd release him.

142
00:08:53,272 --> 00:08:57,044
- Are you disagreeing with me because-
- I'm disagreeing because
that's my medical opinion.

143
00:08:57,116 --> 00:08:59,611
Of course it is.

144
00:08:59,690 --> 00:09:03,257
But unless I've been named as
the fourth part of the "axis of evil,"

145
00:09:03,333 --> 00:09:06,067
invaded and occupied,
this is still not a democracy.

146
00:09:06,141 --> 00:09:10,346
He's staying.
Send for hepatitis serologies
and an autoimmune panel.

147
00:09:13,025 --> 00:09:15,497
[Crying]

148
00:09:21,716 --> 00:09:23,653
Hey, I'm with you.

149
00:09:23,722 --> 00:09:27,721
Old enough to drink,
old enough to do something really stupid
and make yourself a baby.

150
00:09:27,799 --> 00:09:31,502
He's my brother. I'm watching him
while our parents are in Barbados.

151
00:09:31,576 --> 00:09:34,378
He's having trouble breathing,
and there's a lot of wheezing.

152
00:09:34,450 --> 00:09:38,483
Whistling, technically.
Upper airways. Nose.

153
00:09:38,561 --> 00:09:42,094
If he's got the croup, that-
that could become meningitis, right?
Absolutely.

154
00:09:42,171 --> 00:09:45,908
L- I was just studying,
and all of a sudden I hear him crying
and sounding all weird.

155
00:09:45,981 --> 00:09:49,422
Oh- M-My parents
are gonna kill me.

156
00:09:49,490 --> 00:09:52,122
I doubt it.
You don't know them.

157
00:09:52,198 --> 00:09:55,935
No, I doubt you were studying
while your parents were away.

158
00:09:56,009 --> 00:09:58,983
[Whimpering]

159
00:09:59,050 --> 00:10:02,456
Hello, Officer.

160
00:10:02,526 --> 00:10:05,500
You might wanna rinse this off
before you let him play with it again.

161
00:10:07,673 --> 00:10:09,610
[Pager Beeping]

162
00:10:25,053 --> 00:10:27,548
What happened? Where is he?

163
00:10:27,627 --> 00:10:32,698
Vogler called Admitting.
Admitting called Justice.
Justice came and took him away.

164
00:10:32,774 --> 00:10:35,075
And who called Vogler?

165
00:10:42,099 --> 00:10:44,663
He loses money.

166
00:10:44,739 --> 00:10:48,374
So does Ophthalmology.
Who cares? This is a hospital.

167
00:10:48,450 --> 00:10:52,017
- You can't just cut a department.
- You can't control him.

168
00:10:52,093 --> 00:10:55,192
I am the only one that
can control him.

169
00:10:55,268 --> 00:10:57,706
~ D-D-Dr. House in the house ~

170
00:10:57,775 --> 00:10:59,712
Impeccable timing as always.

171
00:10:59,780 --> 00:11:01,944
You had no authority
to release my patient.

172
00:11:02,020 --> 00:11:06,293
My colleague has just informed me
she has a singular talent.

173
00:11:06,365 --> 00:11:09,202
You are just in time
for a demonstration.

174
00:11:10,209 --> 00:11:13,308
Dr. House, from what I understand,

175
00:11:13,384 --> 00:11:16,654
your patient-
From what you understand-
He's not your patient.

176
00:11:16,726 --> 00:11:19,255
How the hell
do you understand anything?
It's sad.

177
00:11:19,333 --> 00:11:25,008
- You're not even a doctor.
- John Smith is here
only because of a court order.

178
00:11:25,082 --> 00:11:27,816
I had the records faxed to the judge.
She rescinded the order.

179
00:11:27,890 --> 00:11:32,300
- Why bother? Just to piss me off?
- Keeping the government off our ass.

180
00:11:32,369 --> 00:11:34,397
[Pager Beeping]
Hmm. Yeah.

181
00:11:34,474 --> 00:11:38,382
- That makes no sense
for a public institution.
- Okay.

182
00:11:38,452 --> 00:11:42,485
- Okay, what?
- Okay, sir.

183
00:11:42,563 --> 00:11:44,500
Carry on.

184
00:11:47,609 --> 00:11:49,546
He really cares about his patients.

185
00:11:49,615 --> 00:11:53,455
Yeah, and he just
walked out of here with nothin'.
Something's up.

186
00:11:54,528 --> 00:11:56,692
Just started vomiting and passed out.

187
00:11:56,767 --> 00:11:59,433
[Woman]
More lidocaine. 590, with epi.

188
00:11:59,509 --> 00:12:04,454
[Man] Thirty-five-year-old male.
Vital signs are stable now.
Gave him two liters en route.

189
00:12:06,293 --> 00:12:09,756
He was just released from here
two hours ago.

190
00:12:09,836 --> 00:12:12,000
You said he was good to go.

191
00:12:12,075 --> 00:12:15,481
Watch that line.
[Man]
He's still not responding.

192
00:12:17,190 --> 00:12:21,098
So, the junior G-man badge
isn't looking so good.

193
00:12:30,926 --> 00:12:33,090
- [Chase] His liver's worse.
- Comatose?

194
00:12:33,166 --> 00:12:35,638
[Cameron] No. Completely different
symptoms than the first time.

195
00:12:35,706 --> 00:12:39,512
His serology tests came back
positive for hepatitis "C."

196
00:12:39,583 --> 00:12:43,286
Hep "C" is a chronic condition.
You don't think
this is an acute situation?

197
00:12:43,360 --> 00:12:45,992
Coma, vomiting, abdominal pain.
Hep "C" explains everything.

198
00:12:46,067 --> 00:12:49,269
- Except for the suddenness of the onset.
- What's wrong with the timing?

199
00:12:49,342 --> 00:12:53,307
You get home one night,
your wife hits you with a baseball bat.

200
00:12:53,387 --> 00:12:57,329
Likely causes:
The fact that you haven't thanked her
for dinner in eight years...

201
00:12:57,398 --> 00:13:01,397
or the receipt for fur handcuffs
that she found in your pants?

202
00:13:01,475 --> 00:13:03,879
Sudden onset
equals approximate cause.

203
00:13:03,948 --> 00:13:08,324
He also has high estrogen levels
in his blood. That's indicative
of a chronic condition, not acute.

204
00:13:08,394 --> 00:13:11,562
One test.
What do his other liver tests tell us?

205
00:13:11,636 --> 00:13:14,735
Normal albumen levels
point toward acute.

206
00:13:14,812 --> 00:13:18,253
Oh, okay, and, uh, why is her test
better than mine?

207
00:13:19,324 --> 00:13:23,130
Because she's cuter,
though it's close.

208
00:13:23,201 --> 00:13:26,573
Do a liver biopsy.
When the results come back,
we'll know what we're looking at.

209
00:13:26,643 --> 00:13:31,053
Why wait to treat the hep "C"?
If I'm right,
Joey gets better that much faster.

210
00:13:31,123 --> 00:13:34,895
Right. Then he gets to testify.
And you get a gold star from Cuddy.

211
00:13:34,966 --> 00:13:38,965
And what's the downside?
Or is that the downside?

212
00:13:39,043 --> 00:13:42,245
Do I have a reason for not
wanting you to get any stars?

213
00:13:44,224 --> 00:13:46,457
Fine. Start the treatment.

214
00:13:46,531 --> 00:13:49,528
It's all your idea.
Don't even mention my name.

215
00:13:49,605 --> 00:13:52,442
There's nothing wrong
with your theory. Go.

216
00:13:55,421 --> 00:13:58,827
But in the "humor me" department,
get a biopsy while you're at it.

217
00:14:02,005 --> 00:14:04,807
Foreman, we need to talk.

218
00:14:11,130 --> 00:14:13,226
- You're off the case.
- What?

219
00:14:13,302 --> 00:14:16,606
- Why?
- Somebody told Vogler that I lied
to the transplant committee.

220
00:14:16,678 --> 00:14:19,378
- You think I did?
- You're too careful.

221
00:14:19,453 --> 00:14:23,395
You wouldn't jump ship unless
you knew what was in the water.
Stop. You're embarrassing me.

222
00:14:23,464 --> 00:14:25,560
But I want Vogler
to think I think it's you.

223
00:14:25,636 --> 00:14:29,203
And I want Cameron and Chase,
Cuddy and Wilson, the nursing staff...

224
00:14:29,280 --> 00:14:31,547
and the cashier in the parking lot
to think that too.

225
00:14:34,459 --> 00:14:35,723
Right.

226
00:14:37,902 --> 00:14:40,739
The blood tests show
you have hepatitis "C."

227
00:14:40,810 --> 00:14:43,282
It's a virus that infects the liver.

228
00:14:43,350 --> 00:14:45,685
No way.
It's not all bad news.

229
00:14:45,757 --> 00:14:49,290
It can often be cured.
And even if not, it's manageable.

230
00:14:49,367 --> 00:14:53,139
How'd my brother get this?
It usually involves
the exchange of bodily fluids. Either-

231
00:14:53,210 --> 00:14:55,705
Bodily fluids?
What are you talkin' about?

232
00:14:55,784 --> 00:14:58,849
There are many ways
the virus can be transmitted-
sharing needles, blood transfusions-

233
00:14:58,926 --> 00:15:02,800
Hey! Nobody talks to my brother
like this, okay?

234
00:15:02,870 --> 00:15:05,000
Fine. No idea how he got it.

235
00:15:05,075 --> 00:15:07,376
But he has hepatitis "C."
We're gonna start him on-

236
00:15:08,886 --> 00:15:14,059
He doesn't have it.
Don't mention it again.
Don't treat him for it.

237
00:15:18,078 --> 00:15:21,450
House has some directed donations,

238
00:15:21,520 --> 00:15:23,457
foundation support-

239
00:15:23,526 --> 00:15:25,463
It's around here.

240
00:15:27,335 --> 00:15:30,172
He makes you miserable.

241
00:15:30,243 --> 00:15:33,114
Eight years he's worked here-
never made a dime for you.

242
00:15:33,185 --> 00:15:35,122
Never listened to you.
He can change. He's-

243
00:15:35,191 --> 00:15:37,755
He hasn't changed in eight years.

244
00:15:37,831 --> 00:15:40,132
Either he can't change,
or you can't change him.

245
00:15:42,610 --> 00:15:46,575
You have no idea how many times
he's lied to you,
undercut your authority,

246
00:15:46,654 --> 00:15:48,784
made you look like crap
to other doctors.

247
00:15:48,861 --> 00:15:53,602
Yes, I hate him,
and here I am desperately trying
to protect his job.

248
00:15:53,673 --> 00:15:56,202
- What does that tell you?
- That you don't hate him.

249
00:15:57,551 --> 00:15:59,749
I do not protect people I like.

250
00:15:59,824 --> 00:16:02,057
I protect people
who are assets to this hospital.

251
00:16:02,130 --> 00:16:05,035
No. That's me.

252
00:16:06,375 --> 00:16:08,505
You-

253
00:16:08,581 --> 00:16:11,145
- You're softer.
- Right.

254
00:16:11,221 --> 00:16:13,955
There are three female
chiefs of medicine...

255
00:16:14,029 --> 00:16:15,966
at major hospitals in this country,

256
00:16:16,034 --> 00:16:18,335
and we all got there
using our feminine wiles.

257
00:16:18,407 --> 00:16:22,042
- It's human nature to want to
protect people we like.
- I don't like him.

258
00:16:22,117 --> 00:16:25,455
To think if wejust form
the right team, we'll all get along
and be able to pull the boat-

259
00:16:25,526 --> 00:16:28,523
- I don't get along with him!
- This is not a team.

260
00:16:28,602 --> 00:16:32,875
It's not a boat.
It's not a machine that has a lot
of parts that have to work together.

261
00:16:32,946 --> 00:16:37,413
The metaphors are all crap.
This is a business. That's all it is.

262
00:16:38,494 --> 00:16:41,662
You like him.
That's bad for business.

263
00:16:47,184 --> 00:16:50,021
[Child Crying]

264
00:16:51,730 --> 00:16:53,290
Oh, this is all my fault.

265
00:16:53,368 --> 00:16:56,205
Took another homework break
with Betty Lou?

266
00:16:56,276 --> 00:16:58,270
No, last week
I showed him a magic trick.

267
00:16:58,348 --> 00:17:02,222
You pulled a quarter
out of his nose.
It's a classic.

268
00:17:02,292 --> 00:17:05,197
Yeah, and now he won't stop
shovin' stuff up there.

269
00:17:05,267 --> 00:17:08,469
- Dr. House.
- Got a crisis here.

270
00:17:09,645 --> 00:17:11,582
It's okay.
[Groans]

271
00:17:11,651 --> 00:17:13,849
[Crying]

272
00:17:16,330 --> 00:17:18,700
Stop!

273
00:17:34,211 --> 00:17:36,148
That's a neat trick.

274
00:17:36,217 --> 00:17:38,154
They have to believe
you'll actually hurt them.

275
00:17:38,222 --> 00:17:40,159
Ah.

276
00:17:46,144 --> 00:17:48,081
Your people insulted my brother.

277
00:17:48,149 --> 00:17:51,590
What, they put Romano in
the Parmesan cheese shaker again?

278
00:17:51,659 --> 00:17:54,291
Said he was a crackhead
or a homo or somethin'.

279
00:17:54,366 --> 00:17:56,303
[Sighs]
Those idiots.

280
00:17:56,371 --> 00:17:59,834
How many times am I gonna have
to send them for sensitivity training?

281
00:17:59,914 --> 00:18:02,854
Nobody's saying he's a homo.
That would be really, really bad.

282
00:18:02,922 --> 00:18:05,417
So let's put a nice, friendly spin on it.

283
00:18:05,496 --> 00:18:08,664
Let's go with, "He got raped in prison."

284
00:18:08,738 --> 00:18:10,675
I saw thejailhouse tats.

285
00:18:10,743 --> 00:18:13,307
Put it together with the blood tests.

286
00:18:14,888 --> 00:18:18,158
There were rumors,
butJoey never said anything about it.

287
00:18:18,230 --> 00:18:21,261
If people find out
he's bein' treated for hep "C"-

288
00:18:23,311 --> 00:18:27,219
Feds get that chart,
someone says somethin'
to somebody, word will get out.

289
00:18:27,289 --> 00:18:30,422
And then Joey's manhood, his rep-
he's destroyed.

290
00:18:33,806 --> 00:18:38,216
You're worried about how his coworkers
will react at the Wal-Mart in Des Moines.

291
00:18:38,284 --> 00:18:41,383
He's not going into Witness Protection.
I'm not gonna let that happen.

292
00:18:43,665 --> 00:18:46,103
Listen, I don't know
if you know about this,

293
00:18:46,173 --> 00:18:49,306
but mob businesses
sometimes keep two sets of books.

294
00:18:49,381 --> 00:18:52,948
- One legit, one not.
- Exactly.

295
00:18:55,665 --> 00:18:57,602
You jerkin' my chain?

296
00:18:57,670 --> 00:19:01,339
Doctors are busy.
Sometimes they forget to write things down.
Happens all the time.

297
00:19:03,185 --> 00:19:05,156
Thanks.

298
00:19:06,227 --> 00:19:08,425
Oh, and, uh,

299
00:19:10,505 --> 00:19:13,502
whatever you're not giving him
for whatever he doesn't have,

300
00:19:13,579 --> 00:19:15,516
is that gonna fix him?

301
00:19:16,789 --> 00:19:18,726
I doubt it.

302
00:19:29,289 --> 00:19:32,126
On your way to polish Vogler's car?

303
00:19:32,197 --> 00:19:34,259
Gone are the days
of the grumpy old doc...

304
00:19:34,336 --> 00:19:37,971
seeing patients in the basement
of his house, getting paid a few chickens.

305
00:19:38,046 --> 00:19:41,613
- How will I eat?
- You know what Cuddy's been
locked away with Vogler about...

306
00:19:41,689 --> 00:19:43,887
all day today and yesterday?

307
00:19:43,962 --> 00:19:45,762
Floor polish costs through the roof?

308
00:19:45,833 --> 00:19:49,639
You. Her secretary's been at
the photocopier all day
with your records.

309
00:19:49,711 --> 00:19:53,448
That's all they're looking at in there.
My car's been stolen.

310
00:19:56,228 --> 00:19:59,099
Or rein-car-nated.

311
00:20:06,088 --> 00:20:08,025
Pink slip.

312
00:20:08,093 --> 00:20:11,796
A gift from the Arnello brothers.

313
00:20:14,979 --> 00:20:18,147
You know, they're gangsters, sure,

314
00:20:18,221 --> 00:20:20,215
but they're thoughtful too.

315
00:20:21,931 --> 00:20:25,771
You can't keep it.
It's... graft.

316
00:20:25,841 --> 00:20:27,971
No, no, no, no. Uh-uh.

317
00:20:28,047 --> 00:20:31,453
Graft is if I tell him I'll only make him
better if he slips me a couple bucks.

318
00:20:31,524 --> 00:20:34,498
Or a payoff for something
I'm not supposed to do.

319
00:20:34,565 --> 00:20:37,562
If I'd asked for the payoff,
which I didn't,

320
00:20:37,640 --> 00:20:39,577
I would've done the bad thing anyway.

321
00:20:39,646 --> 00:20:41,776
So there's nothing wrong with this.

322
00:20:41,852 --> 00:20:43,789
Right.
Damn.

323
00:20:43,857 --> 00:20:46,762
Sixty-five.

324
00:20:46,831 --> 00:20:48,768
Perfectly restored.

325
00:20:48,836 --> 00:20:53,280
What do you think a guy likeJoey
would do if someone turned down a gift?

326
00:20:53,349 --> 00:20:55,947
That's kind of an insult, isn't it?

327
00:20:56,023 --> 00:21:00,194
He might hurt you.
It's definitely possible.

328
00:21:00,268 --> 00:21:03,674
I'm screwed.
Gotta take the car.

329
00:21:09,425 --> 00:21:11,362
[Cameron]
Did you see House's new car?

330
00:21:11,431 --> 00:21:14,371
From Joey.
He obviously can't keep it.

331
00:21:14,439 --> 00:21:17,173
You don't mind the hospital
taking money from Vogler?

332
00:21:17,247 --> 00:21:19,411
That's different. Vogler's legit.

333
00:21:19,487 --> 00:21:23,122
[Scoffs]
That's worse.
Vogler's money came with strings.

334
00:21:23,196 --> 00:21:26,602
Vogler doesn't set me up
to have a mobster take a swing at me.

335
00:21:26,673 --> 00:21:30,810
- I'm sure House didn't know-
- Joey's pressure dropped.

336
00:21:30,884 --> 00:21:33,219
Pushed I.V. Fluids,
now he's holding a hundred systolic.

337
00:21:33,290 --> 00:21:36,526
Septic?
No, it looks like
he's bleeding into his liver.

338
00:21:36,599 --> 00:21:39,197
Varices. See it
with chronic hep "C" all the time.

339
00:21:39,273 --> 00:21:42,110
Biopsy's back.

340
00:21:42,181 --> 00:21:44,585
Two findings. Number one,

341
00:21:44,654 --> 00:21:47,491
lymphocytic infiltrate
and no bridging fibrosis.

342
00:21:47,562 --> 00:21:50,160
Whatever's killing him's
not hep "C." It's acute.

343
00:21:50,236 --> 00:21:52,571
Who said that? I forget.

344
00:21:54,247 --> 00:21:57,984
What are you doing here?
I told you you were off the case.

345
00:21:58,057 --> 00:22:02,866
[Chuckles]
Right. Your diabolic plan to convince
the evil genius he's in the clear,

346
00:22:02,937 --> 00:22:04,965
so he'll let his guard down
and make a fatal mistake.

347
00:22:05,042 --> 00:22:07,844
Sure.
Well, it's clearly
not gonna work now.

348
00:22:07,917 --> 00:22:10,013
What evil genius?

349
00:22:11,092 --> 00:22:14,555
If we knew that,
we wouldn't need a diabolic plan,
would we?

350
00:22:14,635 --> 00:22:19,079
- House thinks someone
ratted him out to Vogler.
- [Chuckles] What, one of us?

351
00:22:19,147 --> 00:22:21,482
No, you guys love me too much.

352
00:22:21,554 --> 00:22:26,055
Look, if it's not the hep "C,"
then what's the problem?
What's causing the liver failure?

353
00:22:26,133 --> 00:22:29,073
Finding number two, toxins.

354
00:22:29,141 --> 00:22:33,551
No. He's only 30 years old,
and his job doesn't expose him
to heavy metals or environmental-

355
00:22:33,620 --> 00:22:35,784
He's a 30-year-old mobster.

356
00:22:35,860 --> 00:22:38,857
He doesn't have a job that results
in accidental exposure to toxins.

357
00:22:38,934 --> 00:22:42,272
He has a job that results
in intentional exposure to toxins.

358
00:22:46,020 --> 00:22:48,960
Someone's poisoned him.

359
00:23:04,603 --> 00:23:07,405
[House]
Whatever this toxin is,
it's doing thejob and fast.

360
00:23:07,477 --> 00:23:09,949
How long till we have
the next round of test results?

361
00:23:10,018 --> 00:23:13,186
- About four hours.
- Too bad his liver's only
gonna last another two.

362
00:23:13,260 --> 00:23:16,028
- We're gonna have to get him a new one.
- What, in two hours?

363
00:23:20,446 --> 00:23:23,283
There is another way.

364
00:23:27,064 --> 00:23:29,058
Relax. It's kosher.

365
00:23:29,136 --> 00:23:31,904
[Snorts]

366
00:23:39,296 --> 00:23:41,494
[Bill]
This is so bizarre.

367
00:23:41,569 --> 00:23:44,337
[Chase]
Not really. We just take
Joey's blood out of his body...

368
00:23:44,411 --> 00:23:46,575
and run it through a pig.

369
00:23:46,650 --> 00:23:51,026
The pig's liver does whatJoey's can't.
It cleans the blood.

370
00:23:51,096 --> 00:23:53,033
Which we send right back to him.

371
00:23:54,806 --> 00:23:56,777
[Bill]
And the pig makes him better?

372
00:23:56,844 --> 00:24:00,377
[Chase]
Nope. Just buys us some time
to figure out what's poisoning your brother.

373
00:24:01,623 --> 00:24:04,620
Like nothin'.
Like you do this all the time.

374
00:24:04,699 --> 00:24:07,764
Oh, we've basically got
a barn in the basement.

375
00:24:15,026 --> 00:24:16,963
[Cameron]
Cross offhemlock.

376
00:24:17,032 --> 00:24:20,097
[Chuckles]
You thought he was being
poisoned by hemlock?

377
00:24:20,174 --> 00:24:22,270
Dr. Euripides tell you
to check for that?

378
00:24:22,347 --> 00:24:24,785
It grows wild by the highways out here.

379
00:24:26,324 --> 00:24:29,126
So, how much do you like House?

380
00:24:30,936 --> 00:24:34,240
- Chase has a big mouth.
- Yeah. He's probably the one
who ratted to Vogler.

381
00:24:34,312 --> 00:24:37,514
- I don't think that he would-
- Does it hurt when you're with House?

382
00:24:37,588 --> 00:24:40,026
Little pain in the tummy,
but it sort of feels good too?

383
00:24:40,094 --> 00:24:43,398
- I don't have the right to show
interest in someone?
- You absolutely do.

384
00:24:43,470 --> 00:24:45,942
And I absolutely have the right
to humiliate you for it.

385
00:24:47,715 --> 00:24:49,652
Anything?

386
00:24:49,720 --> 00:24:54,187
White blood count's low,
probably a result of the illness.
Nothing to connect to the liver.

387
00:24:54,266 --> 00:24:56,203
Is he a smoker?
[Cameron]
Let me check.

388
00:25:01,418 --> 00:25:04,881
Early signs of emphysema.
He's been smoking
at least a dozen years.

389
00:25:04,961 --> 00:25:06,898
[Cameron]
Eighteen. You got that
from the white count?

390
00:25:06,967 --> 00:25:09,337
Nope. Got that from the chest X-ray.

391
00:25:09,407 --> 00:25:11,378
White count just tells me he's quitting.

392
00:25:13,351 --> 00:25:15,288
Two weeks ago.

393
00:25:24,047 --> 00:25:26,485
How's your tummy?

394
00:25:28,826 --> 00:25:30,820
Flat and taut.

395
00:25:30,898 --> 00:25:33,393
[Man]
I've been on thejob for 12 years.

396
00:25:33,472 --> 00:25:37,939
You put $3,000 in your wife's
checking account this morning.
I wanna know where it came from.

397
00:25:38,018 --> 00:25:42,485
I got a perfect record.
Where did you get the money?

398
00:25:42,563 --> 00:25:44,933
Cancel the thumbscrews.
I've got our culprit.

399
00:25:45,002 --> 00:25:47,440
Who?
Not who, "Hu."

400
00:25:47,510 --> 00:25:50,746
- Huh?
- Thanks for playing along.

401
00:25:50,818 --> 00:25:53,815
Chai Hu. Chinese herb
in his "quit smoking" candy.

402
00:25:54,896 --> 00:25:58,200
Reduces cravings.
Also reduces his white blood count.

403
00:25:58,272 --> 00:26:00,573
Oh, yeah, he also took enough
of them to poison himself.

404
00:26:00,645 --> 00:26:03,915
We'll keep him on the pig
for a few more hours,
and then take him off the candy.

405
00:26:03,988 --> 00:26:05,925
He'll be fine.

406
00:26:05,993 --> 00:26:08,830
Pig won't be. Oh, no.

407
00:26:19,362 --> 00:26:22,233
[Groans]
Hey.

408
00:26:25,780 --> 00:26:27,717
Hey, feelin'better?

409
00:26:27,785 --> 00:26:29,779
I'm famished.

410
00:26:29,858 --> 00:26:31,795
I think they got fish sticks
on the menu.

411
00:26:31,863 --> 00:26:35,167
Ah, yeah.
Makes me miss prison.

412
00:26:39,918 --> 00:26:42,288
So, the mobster's good to go?

413
00:26:42,358 --> 00:26:44,420
I'll keep him overnight,
then let the feds know...

414
00:26:44,497 --> 00:26:46,935
he's good to rat out
whoever he wants.

415
00:26:47,004 --> 00:26:49,944
- Brother won't be happy.
- Maybe I have to give back the car.

416
00:26:51,215 --> 00:26:53,687
You should let Vogler tell the feds.
Why?

417
00:26:53,755 --> 00:26:56,319
Because it matters to him.

418
00:26:56,396 --> 00:26:58,994
Because you humiliated him
the first timeJoey was released.

419
00:26:59,069 --> 00:27:02,909
- You think you should still
be in third there, ace?
- He humiliated himself.

420
00:27:02,980 --> 00:27:07,549
And because your job depends
on the kind of mood Vogler's in
at the end of his marathon with Cuddy.

421
00:27:07,626 --> 00:27:11,693
Seriously, man, have you ever
actually driven an automobile before?
There are four gears, you know?

422
00:27:11,770 --> 00:27:15,108
The '66 came with a "shut up" button.

423
00:27:23,335 --> 00:27:26,605
[Chattering]

424
00:27:35,501 --> 00:27:38,566
- [Indistinct]
- [Vogler] I have a problem with the tests.

425
00:27:38,643 --> 00:27:40,841
I need to know-

426
00:27:42,186 --> 00:27:46,630
It is my medical opinion that the patient
is healthy and can be released.

427
00:27:49,539 --> 00:27:51,943
Thanks for letting us know.

428
00:27:56,056 --> 00:27:58,688
Get me the U.S. Attorney's office.

429
00:27:58,764 --> 00:28:02,136
I see you found out
what we're meeting about.
You're having a meeting?

430
00:28:02,207 --> 00:28:05,477
Well, whatever the reason,
the coat looks good on you.

431
00:28:07,186 --> 00:28:09,988
Chai Hu lozenges cause
this kind of liver failure? No way.

432
00:28:10,061 --> 00:28:13,833
Not by themselves.
But in combination with the interferon
it's like gas to a flame.

433
00:28:13,905 --> 00:28:16,434
- What interferon?
- For the hep "C."

434
00:28:16,512 --> 00:28:19,782
- What hep "C"?
- Oops.

435
00:28:19,854 --> 00:28:22,418
Is hiding a mobster's hep "C"
that important?

436
00:28:22,494 --> 00:28:25,434
[Pager Beeping]
Is letting the feds know everything
that important?

437
00:28:25,503 --> 00:28:28,135
You are a piece of work.
Even now, knowing-
Ed-

438
00:28:28,210 --> 00:28:30,477
Edward.

439
00:28:30,550 --> 00:28:33,114
Joey's back in a coma.

440
00:28:38,905 --> 00:28:40,842
[Chase]
He's stable, but comatose.

441
00:28:40,911 --> 00:28:42,848
[Foreman]
Worse than before.
He's on a ventilator.

442
00:28:42,916 --> 00:28:44,853
Question is, why?

443
00:28:46,559 --> 00:28:49,361
It's not his brain.
It's not a toxin.

444
00:28:49,434 --> 00:28:52,032
Our friend Babe
helped with that one.

445
00:28:52,108 --> 00:28:54,204
- So, what else?
- Hep "C."

446
00:28:54,280 --> 00:28:58,724
We never really treated it.
We stopped the interferon
when it started poisoning his liver.

447
00:28:58,792 --> 00:29:02,359
Am I gonna have to write
a song about it?
His chronic hep "C'"...

448
00:29:02,435 --> 00:29:05,033
was not bad enough
to produce these symptoms.

449
00:29:05,110 --> 00:29:08,084
- The estrogen level indicates it is.
- It indicates something else entirely.

450
00:29:08,151 --> 00:29:12,356
We can't give him interferon now.
There are still traces
of the lozenges in his system.

451
00:29:12,429 --> 00:29:14,525
It'll just poison him again.
[Chase]
Genetics.

452
00:29:14,602 --> 00:29:16,596
We don't treat the virus,
we change it.

453
00:29:16,675 --> 00:29:18,976
A nonnucleoside allosteric inhibitor.

454
00:29:19,048 --> 00:29:21,110
It's never been tried on a human being.
It could kill him.

455
00:29:21,186 --> 00:29:24,422
- [Chase] What's the difference?
He's dead without it.
- They're running a trial...

456
00:29:24,495 --> 00:29:27,093
on dogs at St. Sebastian's
out in Philadelphia.

457
00:29:27,169 --> 00:29:29,106
I'll make the call.

458
00:29:30,511 --> 00:29:33,815
What else could cause
his estrogen level to be that high?

459
00:29:36,160 --> 00:29:38,495
Nothing.

460
00:29:42,210 --> 00:29:44,238
[Door Closes]

461
00:29:58,219 --> 00:30:00,156
We're gonna put the medicine in here.

462
00:30:00,225 --> 00:30:03,096
Don't want it to burn his veins
when it goes in.

463
00:30:03,167 --> 00:30:05,138
[Bill]
And you have no idea if it'll work.

464
00:30:05,205 --> 00:30:07,267
[Chase]
It's shown promise in testing.

465
00:30:23,321 --> 00:30:26,055
Ma-Maybe there's nothing up there.
I watched him like a hawk.

466
00:30:26,129 --> 00:30:29,228
- [Crying]
- Pretty sure you didn't.

467
00:30:29,303 --> 00:30:32,277
L- I didn't let him play
with any more little toys.

468
00:30:32,345 --> 00:30:35,342
Thus forcing him
to shove a big one up there.

469
00:30:37,425 --> 00:30:39,760
Stop, or I snap your nose off!

470
00:30:51,062 --> 00:30:52,896
He- He's not too smart.

471
00:30:52,967 --> 00:30:56,408
Genetics is a powerful force.

472
00:31:02,392 --> 00:31:05,798
On the other hand,
maybe he's smarter than you think.

473
00:31:08,309 --> 00:31:10,246
What's goin' on?
Just give me a second.

474
00:31:15,895 --> 00:31:18,128
Always wanted to use one of these.

475
00:31:19,372 --> 00:31:21,366
[Electrical Humming]

476
00:31:25,422 --> 00:31:27,518
Tilt his head back.
L- I don't know. I do-

477
00:31:27,594 --> 00:31:30,362
Just tilt his head back.
[Sighs]

478
00:31:30,435 --> 00:31:32,463
[Clears Throat]

479
00:31:34,146 --> 00:31:36,675
- [Electrical Humming]
- [Boy Cries]

480
00:31:37,922 --> 00:31:40,417
[Clangs]

481
00:31:43,403 --> 00:31:47,311
Nice grasp of concepts.
Relationships. Very smart.

482
00:31:47,381 --> 00:31:49,477
Very cool.

483
00:31:49,554 --> 00:31:52,356
First the policeman, the fireman,
then the fire truck.

484
00:31:52,428 --> 00:31:55,995
Your brother was sending in teams
to save the cat.

485
00:31:56,071 --> 00:31:58,703
[Chuckles]
Wow.

486
00:32:00,549 --> 00:32:03,614
Sometimes the simplest answer-

487
00:32:43,700 --> 00:32:47,267
[Sighs]
What types of comas
do you just snap out of?

488
00:32:47,343 --> 00:32:50,214
He's not snapping out of this one.
He's not improving.

489
00:32:51,287 --> 00:32:54,318
You've crossed out estrogen.
You got an explanation?

490
00:32:54,395 --> 00:32:57,061
Yes, I have, a very simple one.

491
00:32:57,136 --> 00:32:59,768
And?

492
00:32:59,843 --> 00:33:01,905
It's private.

493
00:33:01,982 --> 00:33:04,887
[Clears Throat]

494
00:33:04,957 --> 00:33:08,363
You think I'm the one-
running to Vogler.

495
00:33:09,603 --> 00:33:12,167
You're currently top of the list.

496
00:33:12,243 --> 00:33:14,578
[Sighs]
Toxic comas-

497
00:33:14,650 --> 00:33:18,592
Person's away from the cause
long enough, they recover.

498
00:33:18,660 --> 00:33:22,193
The feds checked for poisons.
We checked for poisons.
I didn't do it.

499
00:33:22,271 --> 00:33:25,336
It's not a poison then.
An allergy.

500
00:33:27,017 --> 00:33:30,584
- Did you hear me?
- What about a food sensitivity?

501
00:33:30,660 --> 00:33:34,899
All his food is strictly controlled.
There's no correlation
between his meals and his condition.

502
00:33:34,971 --> 00:33:37,375
He had steak and potatoes
before the first coma,

503
00:33:37,444 --> 00:33:40,042
and the hospital served fish sticks
before the second one.

504
00:33:43,695 --> 00:33:45,529
You can trust me.

505
00:33:47,839 --> 00:33:51,109
Problem is, if I can't trust you,

506
00:33:51,182 --> 00:33:53,654
I can't trust your statement
that I can trust you.

507
00:33:53,722 --> 00:33:56,593
But thanks anyway.
You've been a big help.

508
00:34:08,662 --> 00:34:11,659
So, where did
you get the money?
What?

509
00:34:11,738 --> 00:34:15,271
Someone paid you off.
What are you talkin' about?

510
00:34:15,347 --> 00:34:17,284
He wasn't poisoned.
You told us that-

511
00:34:17,352 --> 00:34:21,625
[House]
Who's talking about poison?
I'm talking about payoffs, graft.

512
00:34:21,698 --> 00:34:23,931
Leave him alone.

513
00:34:26,677 --> 00:34:29,343
You paid the marshal off.

514
00:34:29,418 --> 00:34:31,651
I didn't pay him to poison my brother.

515
00:34:31,725 --> 00:34:34,220
No. It just worked out that way.

516
00:34:34,298 --> 00:34:37,397
I gave the guy some money
to bring in some decent food.

517
00:34:37,473 --> 00:34:41,245
Better than fish sticks?
I'm thinking steak.

518
00:34:41,317 --> 00:34:43,652
We asked for pasta,
but those stupid feds
could care less-

519
00:34:43,723 --> 00:34:46,024
He had steak before both comas.

520
00:34:46,096 --> 00:34:50,095
Your brother has
ornithine transcarbamylase deficiency.

521
00:34:50,174 --> 00:34:52,703
Want me to write it down?

522
00:34:52,782 --> 00:34:56,815
Good, 'cause it takes a while.
It's genetic, can present at any time.

523
00:34:56,893 --> 00:35:00,390
If the patient eats
a large amount of protein,
especially if he's not used to it-

524
00:35:00,469 --> 00:35:04,571
What, that's it?
He just stays off the red meat,
and he's gonna be fine?

525
00:35:04,647 --> 00:35:07,587
Yes. If I'm right and we stop
the current treatment,
he gets better.

526
00:35:07,655 --> 00:35:11,427
If we stop the current treatment
and I'm wrong, he dies.

527
00:35:11,498 --> 00:35:14,563
- Why would you be wrong?
- His estrogen level.

528
00:35:14,641 --> 00:35:17,239
O.T.D. Doesn't explain
his estrogen level.

529
00:35:17,314 --> 00:35:21,451
But I have a theory.

530
00:35:21,525 --> 00:35:24,396
There is one chemical that,
if ingested,

531
00:35:24,466 --> 00:35:27,736
can cause a person's
estrogen level to increase dramatically.

532
00:35:27,809 --> 00:35:30,977
- What is it?
- It's called estrogen.

533
00:35:32,355 --> 00:35:35,922
Joey's taking estrogen?
What, he wants a sex change?

534
00:35:35,998 --> 00:35:37,935
No, nothing like that.

535
00:35:38,003 --> 00:35:41,604
It's called "Male Flame."

536
00:35:41,680 --> 00:35:46,021
It's probably more
consumer-friendly
in the original Chinese.

537
00:35:46,092 --> 00:35:49,123
It's an herbal aphrodisiac
marketed to gay men.

538
00:35:49,201 --> 00:35:53,109
- Ah, here we go.
- And it's sold on the same Web site
that sells his Chai Hu lozenges.

539
00:35:53,177 --> 00:35:56,208
Guess what's in it?
It starts with an "E."

540
00:35:56,286 --> 00:35:58,758
You wanna get hit too?

541
00:35:58,826 --> 00:36:03,463
That would be quite a trick.
He slapped me so hard,
his brother turned straight.

542
00:36:03,539 --> 00:36:06,980
Joey's a big-time mobster.
Guys like that don't get raped in prison.

543
00:36:07,049 --> 00:36:11,082
They get gifts.
They get food, drugs, cigarettes.

544
00:36:11,160 --> 00:36:13,724
Cable TV.

545
00:36:15,972 --> 00:36:17,909
Joey is not gay.

546
00:36:17,977 --> 00:36:21,349
Maybe not gay, but certainly delightful.

547
00:36:21,420 --> 00:36:27,061
You, on the other hand,
hitting a doctor,
even if it was only Chase,

548
00:36:27,136 --> 00:36:31,135
and asking another one to keep
Joey's chart fresh and homo-free-

549
00:36:31,214 --> 00:36:33,378
that's a bit of an overreaction,
wouldn't you say?

550
00:36:33,453 --> 00:36:37,418
It's almost like you're scared
that it might be true.
You're wrong.

551
00:36:37,498 --> 00:36:40,870
Okay. Then don't
stop the treatment.

552
00:36:43,480 --> 00:36:46,317
But if you're wrong, he dies.

553
00:37:15,199 --> 00:37:17,136
Okay.

554
00:37:32,980 --> 00:37:35,977
He never said anything
to me about it, not once.

555
00:37:39,164 --> 00:37:44,873
That's what I love about you mob guys,
so tolerant of others.

556
00:37:44,945 --> 00:37:46,939
So accepting.

557
00:37:47,018 --> 00:37:51,189
Only way he was coming out
was way, way out.

558
00:37:51,263 --> 00:37:55,365
Lose the tattoos, change his name,
move to another town.

559
00:37:55,441 --> 00:37:58,643
How's a guy like him gonna do that?

560
00:37:58,717 --> 00:38:00,654
Witness Protection.

561
00:38:00,722 --> 00:38:03,753
It's not just for witnesses anymore.

562
00:38:03,831 --> 00:38:06,269
You can go in now,
sit with him if you want.

563
00:38:28,062 --> 00:38:30,694
- How much longer?
- It's only been three hours.

564
00:38:30,769 --> 00:38:35,476
- If it's the O.T.D. -
- If it's the O.T.D.?
What if House is wrong, huh?

565
00:38:35,550 --> 00:38:38,718
That severe a reaction,
it'll take some time-

566
00:38:38,791 --> 00:38:43,132
- He makes these assumptions
about people, talks you into things-
- Mr. Arnello-

567
00:38:43,204 --> 00:38:47,010
He's awake.
He wants to see you.

568
00:38:54,199 --> 00:38:56,136
You look like crap.

569
00:38:56,205 --> 00:39:00,204
That's a joke.
See? I'm sick.
I said you look like crap.

570
00:39:00,283 --> 00:39:02,481
You have no idea
what I just went through out there.

571
00:39:04,427 --> 00:39:07,229
You kept gettin'worse.

572
00:39:07,302 --> 00:39:09,432
And Dr. House kept sayin' all this crap.

573
00:39:10,878 --> 00:39:14,843
You know, if- if I think
you're normal, then he's gonna
keep giving you the medicine.

574
00:39:14,923 --> 00:39:18,022
- If you weren't-
- Weren't what?

575
00:39:20,404 --> 00:39:22,341
Normal?

576
00:39:23,846 --> 00:39:25,783
Yeah.

577
00:39:27,489 --> 00:39:29,426
He said you were a fag.

578
00:39:31,334 --> 00:39:33,601
Witness Protection-
that's your big chance to be one.

579
00:39:37,383 --> 00:39:40,185
- You believed him?
- I don't know what to believe.

580
00:39:40,257 --> 00:39:42,821
You were sick.

581
00:39:42,897 --> 00:39:46,896
I had to make a decision.
I thought you were gonna die.

582
00:39:53,559 --> 00:39:55,894
You believed him.

583
00:39:55,966 --> 00:39:57,903
He stopped the medicine.

584
00:39:59,275 --> 00:40:01,713
Here I am.

585
00:40:09,135 --> 00:40:12,166
- I wanted to talk to you about this.
- There's nothin' to talk about.

586
00:40:18,828 --> 00:40:21,026
You, uh,

587
00:40:21,101 --> 00:40:25,009
ordered some
Chinese Internet health crap,

588
00:40:26,115 --> 00:40:29,089
and they sent the wrong pills,
and you took 'em.

589
00:40:31,161 --> 00:40:33,599
Yeah, yeah. That, uh-

590
00:40:35,573 --> 00:40:38,604
That must be it.

591
00:40:50,246 --> 00:40:52,183
You wanna testify?

592
00:40:53,354 --> 00:40:55,291
Go ahead.

593
00:40:55,360 --> 00:40:58,357
I told the doc. He said it's okay.

594
00:41:00,005 --> 00:41:02,409
- I don't expect you to understand.
- I don't.

595
00:41:07,292 --> 00:41:09,559
All I need to know
is you're my brother, Joey.

596
00:41:12,473 --> 00:41:14,877
If you think this...

597
00:41:14,946 --> 00:41:17,817
thing, whatever,
is gonna make you happy,

598
00:41:22,232 --> 00:41:24,169
then I think you should do it.

599
00:41:28,516 --> 00:41:30,453
You should.

600
00:41:39,479 --> 00:41:41,473
Vogler wants to fire you.

601
00:41:42,487 --> 00:41:45,427
Lose the whole department.

602
00:41:45,495 --> 00:41:48,127
Good thing
you fought for me though, right?

603
00:41:48,202 --> 00:41:52,076
Dress was a nice move,
but you gotta follow it up.

604
00:41:52,146 --> 00:41:54,174
Nasty weekend in Vegas.

605
00:41:54,252 --> 00:41:57,420
Something that shows off
your real administrative skills.

606
00:41:57,494 --> 00:41:59,328
He threatened to fire me.

607
00:42:05,316 --> 00:42:07,583
I'm sorry.

608
00:42:09,727 --> 00:42:12,997
So, how long do I have?
I've got a lot of personal stuff
to pack up.

609
00:42:13,070 --> 00:42:15,132
And I assume you're gonna
want to throw a party.

610
00:42:15,208 --> 00:42:17,179
I told him I know
where the bodies are buried.

611
00:42:17,248 --> 00:42:21,817
The stuff he needs to know
that's not in the books.
I told him he can't ditch me.

612
00:42:21,894 --> 00:42:24,458
He's only keeping you on
because you know the secret handshakes.

613
00:42:24,534 --> 00:42:27,906
He's a quick study.
Six months, he'll have the moves down.
He won't need you anymore.

614
00:42:27,976 --> 00:42:30,916
- I'll deal with that then.
- So I stay.

615
00:42:30,984 --> 00:42:33,752
Yes.

616
00:42:33,826 --> 00:42:36,059
But some things are going to change.

617
00:42:37,235 --> 00:42:40,539
Profits. New world order.

618
00:42:40,611 --> 00:42:43,676
Everything's about profits.
Yeah, that's real new.

619
00:42:43,752 --> 00:42:47,660
You could rent out the Corvette
every once in a while
or lend it to a friend.

620
00:42:47,730 --> 00:42:50,134
That would be easy,
and it would be wrong.

621
00:42:50,203 --> 00:42:52,003
But Cuddy stood up for you.

622
00:42:52,075 --> 00:42:54,046
[Sighs]
To a point.

623
00:42:54,114 --> 00:42:56,051
To what point?

624
00:42:56,119 --> 00:42:59,856
I gotta do six more
clinic hours a month.
So do two of them.

625
00:43:00,932 --> 00:43:03,769
Why only two?

626
00:43:03,840 --> 00:43:05,777
'Cause one of them's gone.

627
00:43:07,216 --> 00:43:09,312
I gotta fire somebody.

628
00:43:25,800 --> 00:43:27,737
Good morning.

629
00:44:12,392 --> 00:44:13,656
That's some bad hat, Harry.

9999
00:00:0,500 --> 00:00:2,00
<font color="#ffff00" size=14>www.tvsubtitles.net</font>
